<title>USA: Viacom completes sale of radio stations.</title>
<headline>Viacom completes sale of radio stations.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Viacom Inc on Wednesday said it completed the sale of the Viacom Radio Group to Evergreen Media Corp and Chancellor Broadcasting Co for $1.075 billion in cash.</p>
<p>Viacom said it planned to use proceeds from the sale, announced in February 1997, to repay debt.</p>
<p>Viacom Radio Group consists of 10 stations in five major markets, including multiple FM stations in the single markets of New York, Los Angeles and Washington.</p>
<p>Evergreen has agreed to merge with Chancellor, with the combined entity to be named Chancellor Media Corp.</p>
</text>
